---
// src/pages/privacy.astro
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const lastUpdated = "September 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — CloudGrid Africa"
  description="How CloudGrid Africa collects, uses, and protects personal data on cloudgridafrica.com, in line with the Kenya Data Protection Act 2019."
>
  <Navbar />
  <main id="main-content" class="pt-32 pb-24">
    <div class="cga-container">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
        <p class="cga-eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[13px] text-ink-muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

        <div class="prose prose-invert prose-headings:font-semibold prose-headings:tracking-tight prose-headings:text-white prose-p:text-[14.5px] prose-p:leading-relaxed prose-p:text-ink-secondary prose-a:text-signal-blue prose-a:no-underline hover:prose-a:underline prose-strong:text-ink-primary prose-li:text-ink-secondary prose-hr:border-midnight-border mt-10 max-w-none">
          <p>
            <em>
              This policy is provided as a plain-language reference for visitors to
              cloudgridafrica.com. It is not a substitute for legal advice, and CloudGrid
              Africa recommends independent legal review before relying on it for
              compliance purposes beyond this website.
            </em>
          </p>

          <h2>Who we are</h2>
          <p>
            CloudGrid Africa ("we", "us") is a cloud and cybersecurity engineering firm
            based in Westlands, Nairobi, Kenya, co-located at Raxio Data Centre Nairobi.
            We are the data controller for personal data collected through
            cloudgridafrica.com. Contact us at
            <a href="mailto:hello@cloudgridafrica.com">hello@cloudgridafrica.com</a> or
            +254 721 656 835 for any privacy question.
          </p>

          <h2>What we actually collect on this site</h2>
          <p>We keep this section specific to what this website does, not a generic list:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Contact form (/#contact):</strong> your name, work email, and the
              message you submit. Sent to us via <a href="https://resend.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Resend</a>,
              our transactional email provider, and to our inbox at hello@cloudgridafrica.com.
              We use this solely to respond to your enquiry.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Chat widget:</strong> messages you type into the chat widget are sent
              to Anthropic's Claude API to generate a response. We do not attach your name,
              email, or any other identifying information to these messages unless you type
              it yourself. Conversation history is kept only in your browser's memory for
              that visit — it is not stored on our servers and disappears when you close or
              reload the page.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Live weather &amp; time display:</strong> the "Live Systems Strip" on
              our homepage fetches current Nairobi weather from
              <a href="https://open-meteo.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open-Meteo</a>.
              This is a fixed location lookup (Nairobi's coordinates) — no data about you or
              your device is sent to Open-Meteo.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Performance and traffic analytics:</strong> we use Vercel Web
              Analytics and Vercel Speed Insights to understand aggregate visitor numbers
              and page performance. Both are designed to operate without setting tracking
              cookies and without building an individual profile of you across other sites.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Cookies</h2>
          <p>
            This site does not use cookies for advertising or cross-site tracking. Some
            interface preferences — such as whether you've dismissed the cookie notice —
            are stored using your browser's local storage rather than a cookie. This
            information stays on your device and is never transmitted to us.
          </p>

          <h2>Legal basis for processing</h2>
          <p>
            Under the Kenya Data Protection Act 2019, we process the data described above
            on the basis of your consent (submitting the contact form or using the chat
            widget is a voluntary action) and our legitimate interest in responding to
            business enquiries and operating a functioning website.
          </p>

          <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
          <p>
            Contact form submissions and their associated email threads are retained for as
            long as reasonably necessary to manage the business relationship, and are
            deleted or anonymised when no longer needed. Chat widget conversations are not
            retained by us at all beyond the browser session in which they occur.
          </p>

          <h2>Your rights under Kenya DPA 2019</h2>
          <p>You have the right to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Be informed of how your data is used (this policy).</li>
            <li>Access the personal data we hold about you.</li>
            <li>Request correction of inaccurate data.</li>
            <li>Request deletion of your data, subject to legal retention requirements.</li>
            <li>Object to processing based on legitimate interest.</li>
            <li>Lodge a complaint with the Office of the Data Protection Commissioner (ODPC), Kenya.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            To exercise any of these rights, email
            <a href="mailto:hello@cloudgridafrica.com">hello@cloudgridafrica.com</a>.
          </p>

          <h2>Data security</h2>
          <p>
            This site is served exclusively over HTTPS, enforces a strict
            Content-Security-Policy, and never exposes API keys or credentials to your
            browser — every integration with a third-party service (email, AI chat,
            weather) is proxied through our own server-side infrastructure. Internally, we
            apply the same engineering standards we deliver to clients.
          </p>

          <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this policy as the site changes. Material changes will be
            reflected in the "Last updated" date above.
          </p>

          <hr />
          <p>
            Questions about this policy? <a href="/#contact">Contact us</a> or read our
            <a href="/terms">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
